{
 "_comment": "The decks the game ships, as lists over cards.json: a starter deck (starter: true) is what a new profile gets, none while the cards change (Martin, 2026-10-29: back once they settle); a bot deck (bot: true) is what the bots play, ranked and in Practice's Random (a starter may be both). Starter decks share no card, so a new player meets as many cards as possible; bot decks may overlap with anything (Martin, 2026-10-19). Each deck: slug, name, cover (the card whose art faces it), order (the menus), cards (id: copies; a legal 4-4-6 list of collectible cards). Edited here by hand, or a starter's through tools/cards/hq.py (move, deck-name). The leaders prototype (branch leaders): a deck may name its leader (leader: a card id in its list, engine/leaders.py); the decks named by a leader are the bot decks' variants for it. Martin's new pool (2026-11-16): the bots play the six pool_N decks, numbered until he names them; the older lists stay, unplayed by the bots.",
